      "extract": "2 STEVE BRYSON, M. H. FREEDMAN, Z.-X. HE, AND ZHENGHAN WANG Theorem B. If K is a smooth prime (not a connected sum) knot, then there exists a simple closed rectiﬁable γK of knot type K with E(γK) ≤E(γ) for all rectiﬁable loops γ which are topologically ambient isotopic to K. Theorem C. Any minimizer γK, as above, will enjoy some regularity. With an arc length parametrization, γK will be in C1,1. Several results of",
